m=A.eh(l,a2,"ai","For Indian software developers and freelancers, API bills in US Dollars with 20% TCS/GST deductions can eat into margins rapidly. DeepSeek has emerged as the go-to alternative, offering exceptional reasoning on Python, Dart, and TypeScript codebases.\n\n### Connecting in VS Code via Continue.dev\n1. Install the open-source **Continue** extension in VS Code.\n2. Generate your DeepSeek API key from platform.deepseek.com.\n3. Add the custom endpoint in `config.json`.\n4. Test full-codebase refactoring and automatic test generation.\n      ","DeepSeek offers near-Claude 3.5 Sonnet coding performance at 1/10th the token pricing. Here is how to configure it in VS Code and Cursor using Indian credit cards without Forex markup.",A.b([],c7),"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","art-9",!1,!1,!0,j,k,6,"deepseek-coder-v2-complete-setup-guide-for-indian-developers","Coding Copilots",c2,"DeepSeek-V2 for Indian Developers: Free High-Performance Coding AI Setup",A.b([B.GW],c8),m,22100)
